input:
void bubble_sort(std::vector<int>& arr) {
    bool swapped;
    do {
        swapped = false;
        for (size_t i = 0; i < arr.size() - 1; ++i) {
            if (arr[i] > arr[i + 1]) {
                std::swap(arr[i], arr[i + 1]);
                swapped = true;
            }
        }
    } while (swapped);
}

output:
#include <algorithm>

void optimized_sort(std::vector<int>& arr) {
    std::sort(arr.begin(), arr.end());
}
---
Replaced manual Bubble Sort O(N^2) with std::sort (Introsort), which is O(N log N). std::sort is highly optimized, hybridizing QuickSort, HeapSort, and Insertion Sort to guarantee worst-case performance far superior to Bubble Sort.

